        <mxCell id="100" parent="1" vertex="1" value="&lt;b style=&quot;font-size:14px&quot;&gt;Availability tests: what they probe and why&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Probes:&lt;/b&gt; https://&amp;lt;site&amp;gt;.azurestaticapps.net/healthz.html. Inside the VNet the name resolves, through the Private DNS zone, to the private endpoint, so the request never leaves the private network.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why a probe of our own:&lt;/b&gt; public network access is off, so Azure's internet web tests cannot reach the site from any region. A scheduled Container Apps job inside the VNet does the checking instead.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why /healthz.html:&lt;/b&gt; it is the only page without sign-in. Every other page redirects to the APEX Entra login.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;How:&lt;/b&gt; one job run every 5 minutes (probe_cron), curl GET with a 30 s timeout, no retries. The job uses the azure-cli image from MCR only for bash, curl and awk; the script is probe.sh.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Passes when:&lt;/b&gt; HTTP 200. A timeout, connection error or invalid certificate is recorded as HTTP 000, a failure.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Result:&lt;/b&gt; an availability record (test name, success, duration, location vnet-&amp;lt;region&amp;gt;) is written to Application Insights over Monitor Private Link, in the same table internet web tests use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alerts:&lt;/b&gt; severity 1 when availability drops below 90% over 5 minutes (with one run per 5 minutes, one failed run is enough). Severity 1 &quot;probe silent&quot; when no result arrives for 15 minutes: the probe itself or its network path is down.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Does not prove:&lt;/b&gt; that sign-in works, that users can reach the site over VPN or ExpressRoute (it tests from inside the VNet only), or that the certificate is far from expiry (no 14-day warning; one location, not five)." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f6f4;strokeColor=#a8a49d;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;fontColor=#1c1c1c;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="1025" width="700" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="101" parent="1" edge="1" value="" source="100" target="15" style="html=1;edgeStyle=none;endArrow=none;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;strokeColor=#8a8781;strokeWidth=1.2;exitX=0.464;exitY=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryPerimeter=0;">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
